(text "Notes" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 255.6 32.4 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e54caa8f-7092-5e55-b31d-8c65a3dbd1a0"))
(text "Main current path" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 255.6 39.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ed82edeb-bb1d-5aa8-a773-64b0b3538a29"))
(text "BT1 + -> F1 40 A -> J1 -> K1 stud A -> K1 stud B\n-> TB2 -> B+ of U10-U14 (10 AWG).\nB- of U10-U14 -> TB1 star -> J1 -> BT1 -.\nThe blade fuse block carries only the small\nbranches; it is not in the 40 A path.\nK1 precharge: decide after the bench test\n(5 x 470 µF behind a 125 A contactor)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 255.6 42.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8819710d-d115-52e4-a842-50595849e7ac"))
(text "Fuse rule" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 255.6 63.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8769fee9-2bb8-5cb8-934d-b885af937cf0"))
(text "Every fuse protects the wire after it:\nthe wire is rated above the fuse.\nF1 40 A: 10 AWG. F2 15 A: 14 AWG.\nF6 10 A: 16 AWG. F3-F5, F7, F8: 20 AWG\nor heavier. See WIRE_LIST.md." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 255.6 66.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3cb0b8ec-4a1f-5e43-825d-ae14536b9bfc"))
